==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|unnanan|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old Saxon ''[[unnan]]'', Old High German ''unnan'', Middle Dutch ''[[onnen]]'', Old Norse ''[[unna]]'' (Icelandic, Norwegian, Swedish ''[[unna]]'', Danish ''[[unde]]'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈunːɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=pretpres}}

# to [[grant]] or [[bestow]] (+ ''dat'' (person) + ''gen'' (thing))
# to [[wish]]
# to [[intercede]]

====Conjugation====
{{ang-conj|type=pretpres||ann|*anst|ann|unnon|unne|unnen|ūþe|ūþest|ūþe|ūþon|ūþe|ūþen|*unne|*unnaþ|unnende|unnen}}

====Descendants====
* Middle English: [[unne]]

